Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
The missing piece -- the escape-probability weight correction\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ea9cb103-c78e-40d2-912a-6a5e0875e48d"],

Cell["\<\
exitProbDist/ePDFx/eCDFx above give the corrected sampling distribution for \
the exit direction, assuming escape is certain. But a walk sampled from the \
ordinary mixed classical/Dwivedi-guided scheme has no such guarantee. \
Substituting the corrected direction in without correcting for that mismatch \
introduces a bias equal to exactly how likely the original scheme was to have \
escaped from this same depth. This section works that probability out, so the \
resampled contribution can be divided by it and come out unbiased.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7a1f2e72-85d6-49f0-9519-be08387b1bf7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Classical (unguided) escape probability -- closed form", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"c4ebdf3c-7be0-4e71-8b0d-a2b60e621896"],

Cell["\<\
P(escape | classical sampling, depth x) = Integrate[(1/2) Exp[x/u], \
{u,-1,0}], which reduces exactly to (1/2) E2(x) via u -> -1/s.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d0722f2-7518-4149-9d53-6f2ae32fa4ab"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
PescClassical[x_?NumericQ]:=(1/2) ExpIntegralE[2,N[x]];

(* sanity check: numeric value at a few depths *)
Table[{x, PescClassical[x] // N}, {x, {0.2, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 5.0}}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996660848002322*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[272]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b49da841-2667-4ba6-926c-0116998dd401"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0.2`", ",", "0.28710032212060155`"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0.5`", ",", "0.16332193116227653`"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1.`", ",", "0.07424775338796104`"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2.`", ",", "0.01876713091024522`"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"5.`", ",", "0.0004982345213544193`"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.996339920195881*^9, 3.9966604563014975`*^9, 
  3.996660851671108*^9, 3.9966609886101847`*^9, 3.9966613587043247`*^9, 
  3.996662802776842*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[275]=",ExpressionUUID->"03b42cec-8802-47df-9f3b-64192f3a321f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Dwivedi-guided escape probability -- no closed form, quadrature\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fd81ec94-d4e2-42ec-a2e1-cf076e810571"],

Cell["\<\
Same u-convention as exitProbDist/ePDFx above (u<0 = toward escape). nu0 is \
the Dwivedi diffusion length; phaseLog = Log[(nu0+1)/(nu0-1)]. The guided \
direction density (normalized on u in [-1,1]) is 1/((nu0+u) phaseLog); the \
guided distance-stretching factor for direction u is (1+u/nu0); the geometric \
distance to the boundary from depth x along direction u is -x/u. This was \
derived independently in the code's own (opposite-sign) convention and \
confirmed to match this notebook-convention version exactly, numerically, \
before being trusted.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"91d60621-2afe-4bde-bbfc-9c6a548979e9"],

Cell["\<\
PescDwivedi[x_?NumericQ,nu0_?NumericQ]:=Module[{phaseLog,xn=N[x],nu0n=N[nu0]},\
phaseLog=Log[(nu0n+1)/(nu0n-1)];
NIntegrate[(1/((nu0n+u) \
phaseLog))*Exp[xn/u+xn/nu0n],{u,-1,0},Method\[Rule]\"GaussKronrodRule\"]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9966608868049393`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "In[276]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c7646f9b-527b-4036-90ba-d4d337631751"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
The actual scheme's escape probability, and the unbiased resampled weight\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"a2f532b4-6792-4a4c-92a6-4d98aee053f6"],

Cell["\<\
PescMix is the escape probability under whichever mixture of classical and \
guided sampling the walk actually uses. resampledWeight is the corrected, \
unbiased contribution: the ordinary transmittance to the resampled exit \
point, divided by the corrected direction's own density (ePDFx), divided \
again by PescMix -- this second division is the piece that was missing.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2d771190-c03b-4047-91ff-670021f61a66"],

Cell["\<\
PescMix[x_?NumericQ,nu0_?NumericQ,guidedFraction_?NumericQ]:=
(1-guidedFraction) PescClassical[x]+guidedFraction PescDwivedi[x,nu0]

resampledWeight[transR_?NumericQ,x_?NumericQ,uR_?NumericQ,nu0_?NumericQ,\
guidedFraction_?NumericQ]:=
transR/(ePDFx[x,uR]*PescMix[x,nu0,guidedFraction])\
\>", "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9966609060260572`*^9, 3.9966609192230577`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[277]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3d94fb4c-0ff5-41e9-a438-f19daa19d204"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Sanity checks", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6d8d3f2a-e101-4048-9317-3690ddb2f8b1"],

Cell["\<\
Two checks worth actually running. 
First: PescMix should reduce exactly to PescClassical in the guidedFraction \
-> 0 limit (trivial, but worth confirming the wiring). 
Second, more meaningful: as nu0 -> Infinity (weak guiding, approaching the \
classical limit), PescDwivedi itself should also approach PescClassical, \
since an infinitely long diffusion length means the guided distribution stops \
actually guiding toward anything in particular.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.996661178582631*^9, 
  3.9966611834313345`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"41e02577-50bb-4e9a-85eb-\
9b9291aa2f77"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"check", " ", "1"}], ":", 
     RowBox[{"trivial", " ", 
      RowBox[{"reduction", "--"}], " ", "now", " ", "numeric"}]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
    "so", " ", "it", " ", "actually", " ", "exercises", " ", "PescDwivedi", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"evaluated", ",", 
       RowBox[{"then", " ", "multiplied", " ", "by", " ", "0"}]}], ")"}], " ",
      "rather", " ", "than", " ", "skipping", " ", "it", " ", "entirely", " ",
      "the", " ", "way", " ", "the", " ", "purely", " ", "symbolic", " ", 
     "version", " ", "did"}]}], "*)"}], 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PescMix", "[", 
     RowBox[{"1.0", ",", "2.0", ",", "0"}], "]"}], "\[Equal]", 
    RowBox[{"PescClassical", "[", "1.0", "]"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", "\n", 
   RowBox[{"(*", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"check", " ", "2"}], ":", 
      RowBox[{
      "PescDwivedi", " ", "should", " ", "approach", " ", "PescClassical", 
       " ", "as", " ", "nu0"}]}], "\[Rule]", "Infinity"}], "*)"}], 
   "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"nu0", ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"PescDwivedi", "[", 
          RowBox[{"1.0", ",", 
           RowBox[{"N", "[", "nu0", "]"}]}], "]"}], "//", "N"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"PescClassical", "[", "1.0", "]"}], "//", "N"}]}], "}"}], 
      ",", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"nu0", ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", "10", ",", "100", ",", "1000"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], 
     "]"}], "//", "TableForm"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9966607791026707`*^9, 3.9966607791026707`*^9}},
 CellLabel->
  "In[280]:=",ExpressionUUID->"df241843-f2e5-4cfd-917d-30f1e6b9362e"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
